meta {
  name: dms auth and routing
  seq: 3
}

docs {
  # Ed-Fi API v8 (DMS) authorization checks

  Run with the dms environment after the main collection:
  `bru run tests -r --env-file environments/dms.bru && bru run tests-dms -r --env-file environments/dms.bru`

  Each request gets its own tokens from the DMS token endpoint (one per client per run; the
  self-contained identity provider allows 15 active tokens per client). Wrong-audience and
  expired tokens need the Configuration Service's signing key to mint, so they are covered by
  tests/unit-tests/token-verifier.test.js instead.
}
